1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,810
A positive test,
but only a 9% chance it's real?

2
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:05,198
Here are 1,000 people

3
00:00:05,248 --> 00:00:07,368
10 of them have the disease (1%)

4
00:00:07,418 --> 00:00:11,026
An imaginary test: always positive if you're sick,
but 10% of healthy people test positive by mistake

5
00:00:11,076 --> 00:00:14,796
Let's gather everyone who tested positive

6
00:00:14,846 --> 00:00:17,166
Even with a positive result, it's only about a 9% chance!

7
00:00:17,216 --> 00:00:20,136
There are so many healthy people
that a 10% mistake rate alone means 99 people

8
00:00:20,186 --> 00:00:22,806
What if we test just those 109 again?

9
00:00:22,856 --> 00:00:26,076
Two positives — it jumps to 50%!

10
00:00:26,126 --> 00:00:29,776
Counting again "among the people who tested positive" —
that's conditional probability

11
00:00:30,776 --> 00:00:34,526
NEXT: Is the dot product
a shadow's length?
